{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>אוֹ אָז יִכָּנַע לְבָבָם הֶעָרֵל</b> — like 'אוֹ נוֹדַע כִּי שׁוֹר נַגָּח הוּא' (Exodus 21:36). Another interpretation: perhaps — maybe then their uncircumcised heart will be humbled. <b>וְאָז יִרְצוּ אֶת עֲוֹנָם</b> — they will make atonement for their iniquity through their sufferings; this is the language of Rashi. But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that He says: 'וְהֵבֵאתִי אֹתָם בְּאֶרֶץ אֹיְבֵיהֶם' — either until the time when their uncircumcised heart is humbled, or until the time when they accept their iniquity, throughout the length of the exile. Now, after 'וְהִתְוַדּוּ אֶת עֲוֹנָם' (Leviticus 26:40), it would have been fitting for Him to say immediately 'וְזָכַרְתִּי אֶת בְּרִיתִי יַעֲקֹב' (Leviticus 26:42), for what reason is there to say 'וְהֵבֵאתִי אֹתָם בְּאֶרֶץ אֹיְבֵיהֶם' at this point, since this is not now the time that He exiles them and brings them into the land of their enemies? Rabbi Abraham explained: I too have done this with them, and I have chastised them in order to bring them into the land of their enemies to humble their uncircumcised heart, and He mentioned this here because they confessed their iniquity for the purpose that I am the one who orchestrates it for them, for even at the time of their corruption I intended concerning them that they should repent and confess. In my opinion, He hints that after their confession He will deal with them בְּקֶרִי (contrarily), and He will bring them again into the land of their enemies until their uncircumcised heart is humbled, and this is a hint that He brought them into the land but it was not conquered before them; rather, they had adversaries and enemies there, as it says 'וַיֹּאמְרוּ צָרֵנוּ' (Nehemiah 4:5), 'וַיְהִי כַּאֲשֶׁר שָׁמְעוּ אוֹיְבֵינוּ' (Nehemiah 4:9), and the land was in the hands of the nations, as Ezra said in his prayer: 'הִנֵּה אֲנַחְנוּ הַיּוֹם עֲבָדִים וְהָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר נָתַתָּ לַאֲבֹתֵינוּ לֶאֱכֹל אֶת פִּרְיָהּ וְאֶת טוּבָהּ הִנֵּה אֲנַחְנוּ עֲבָדִים עָלֶיהָ וּתְבוּאָתָהּ מַרְבָּה לַמְּלָכִים אֲשֶׁר נָתַתָּ עָלֵינוּ בְּחַטֹּאותֵינוּ וְעַל גְּוִיֹּתֵינוּ מֹשְׁלִים וּבִבְהֶמְתֵּנוּ כִּרְצוֹנָם וּבְצָרָה גְדוֹלָה אֲנָחְנוּ' (Nehemiah 9:36–37)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:01:08.551096858Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}